/*
class Node
    {
        int data;
        Node next;
        Node(int d) {
            data = d;
            next = null; 
        }
    }
*/

class Solution {
Node removeDuplicates(Node head) {
        
        if (head == null) { return null; }          // Base case: empty list  
        Node cur = head;                            // Start from head
                
        while (cur != null && cur.next != null) {   // Traverse till second last node
            
            if (cur.data == cur.next.data) {        // Duplicate found
                cur.next = cur.next.next;           // Skip the duplicate node
            }
            else {
                cur = cur.next;                     // Move to next distinct node
            }
        }
              
        return head;                                // Return modified head
    }
}

//////////////////////// DRY RUN /////////////////////////////

Input: 1 -> 1 -> 2 -> 3 -> 3 -> 4 -> null

ORIGINAL LIST (Before Removal):

[1|•] -> [1|•] -> [2|•] -> [3|•] -> [3|•] -> [4|•] -> null
 ^
cur


ITERATION WALKTHROUGH:

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Iteration 1: cur = 1 (first node)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        cur.data = 1, cur.next.data = 1
        1 == 1 → DUPLICATE FOUND
        
        Action: cur.next = cur.next.next
                (Skip the second 1)
        
        Before: [1|•] -> [1|•] -> [2|•] -> [3|•] -> [3|•] -> [4|•] -> null
                 ^        ^
               cur     cur.next
        
        After:  [1|•] -----------> [2|•] -> [3|•] -> [3|•] -> [4|•] -> null
                 ^
               cur
               (second 1 is removed)


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Iteration 2: cur = 1 (still at first node)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        cur.data = 1, cur.next.data = 2
        1 != 2 → NO DUPLICATE
        
        Action: cur = cur.next (move forward)
        
        [1|•] -> [2|•] -> [3|•] -> [3|•] -> [4|•] -> null
                 ^
               cur


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Iteration 3: cur = 2
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        cur.data = 2, cur.next.data = 3
        2 != 3 → NO DUPLICATE
        
        Action: cur = cur.next (move forward)
        
        [1|•] -> [2|•] -> [3|•] -> [3|•] -> [4|•] -> null
                          ^
                        cur


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Iteration 4: cur = 3 (first 3)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        cur.data = 3, cur.next.data = 3
        3 == 3 → DUPLICATE FOUND
        
        Action: cur.next = cur.next.next
                (Skip the second 3)
        
        Before: [1|•] -> [2|•] -> [3|•] -> [3|•] -> [4|•] -> null
                           ^        ^
                         cur     cur.next
        
        After:  [1|•] -> [2|•] -> [3|•] -----------> [4|•] -> null
                           ^
                         cur
               (second 3 is removed)


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Iteration 5: cur = 3 (still at first 3)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        cur.data = 3, cur.next.data = 4
        3 != 4 → NO DUPLICATE
        
        Action: cur = cur.next (move forward)
        
        [1|•] -> [2|•] -> [3|•] -> [4|•] -> null
                                   ^
                                 cur


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Iteration 6: cur = 4 (last node)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        cur.next = null → Loop terminates
        
        No more nodes to compare


FINAL LIST (After Removal):

[1|•] -> [2|•] -> [3|•] -> [4|•] -> null
 ^
head


Output: 1 -> 2 -> 3 -> 4


SUMMARY TABLE:

Iteration    cur.data    cur.next.data    Action                      List State
---------    --------    -------------    ------                      ----------
1            1           1                Skip duplicate (remove 2nd)  1->2->3->3->4
2            1           2                Move cur forward             1->2->3->3->4
3            2           3                Move cur forward             1->2->3->3->4
4            3           3                Skip duplicate (remove 2nd)  1->2->3->4
5            3           4                Move cur forward             1->2->3->4
6            4           null             Loop ends                    1->2->3->4


KEY LOGIC:

• Only move cur forward when NO duplicate is found
• When duplicate found, skip it but DON'T move cur (check new next node)
• Works because list is SORTED (duplicates are always adjacent)


//////////////////////// QUESTION ////////////////////////////

Remove Duplicates from Sorted Linked List

Given the head of a sorted singly linked list, remove all duplicate elements such that each element appears only once. Return the head of the modified sorted linked list.

Examples:

Input:  1 -> 1 -> 2 -> 3 -> 3
Output: 1 -> 2 -> 3

Input:  2 -> 2 -> 2 -> 2 -> 2
Output: 2

Input:  1 -> 2 -> 3 -> 4
Output: 1 -> 2 -> 3 -> 4 (no duplicates)

Constraints:
- 0 <= number of nodes <= 300
- 0 <= node->data <= 100
- List is sorted in non-decreasing order

Time Complexity: O(n) - single pass
Space Complexity: O(1) - no extra space used
